{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310652,"nonce":"AloSo5KtFyiQXrO2dDYMp/6UdJE=","title":"Haxe 4.2 module-level fields (`function f()` outside a class) need FOUR layers, not one. Triage called it contained; it is not. Each ...","message":"**Module-level fields do not work.** Haxe 4.2 allows statics declared outside\nany class; rayzor reports `[E0200] Cannot find name 'helper'`.\n\n```haxe\nfunction helper() { return 5; }\nclass M { static function main() { Sys.println(helper()); } }   // E0200\nprivate var counter = 7;                                        // E0200\ninline function twice(x:Int) { return x * 2; }                  // E0200\n```\n\n11 corpus tests. Triage rated this **contained**. It is NOT — attempted\n2026-08-28 and fully reverted.\n\n\n1. **Scope binding.** `ast_lowering/decls/mod.rs::lower_module_field` calls\n   `symbol_table.create_variable(name)` and never puts the symbol in a scope.\n   Adding it to `scope_tree` DOES NOT WORK: `resolve_symbol_in_scope_hierarchy`\n   asks `symbol_table.lookup_symbol(scope, name)`, which is keyed by scope in\n   the SYMBOL TABLE. Use `create_variable_in_scope(name, current_scope)`.\n   -\u003e resolution then succeeds.\n2. **HIR lowering.** `ir/tast_to_hir.rs::lower_module_field` was a `// TODO`\n   stub that dropped the field entirely. Implement it inserting into\n   `module.functions` / `module.globals`, keyed by the FIELD's symbol (the one\n   the call resolves to), overwriting `hir_func.symbol_id` to match.\n   -\u003e the function reaches MIR: `fn @main.helper [name=helper]() -\u003e void`.\n3. **Return type.** `decls/fields.rs::lower_function_object` defaults an\n   unannotated return to `void_type()` instead of inferring from the body, so\n   the body returned i32 from a `-\u003e void` signature and the caller read\n   nothing. Lower the body FIRST, then `infer_return_type_from_body`.\n   -\u003e and this is where it went from silent-empty to **SIGSEGV**.\n4. Unresolved: something after that still faults. Not diagnosed.\n\n\nEach partial step made the failure QUIETER then WORSE:\nloud E0200 -\u003e exit 0 printing nothing -\u003e exit 139.\n\nThat is different from shipping a fix that exposes a pre-existing defect (the\n`inline` / `abstract class` parser work, which was right to ship). Here the\nregression was introduced BY the half-built feature. Surfacing someone else's\nbug is good; manufacturing a silent wrong answer is not.\n\nDo this properly end to end, with the `fn`/`var`/`inline fn` repros above as the\ngate, or not at all.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_module_level_fields_need_four_layers` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}